{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HFiH9dE8UQJ8nYzoc2pzvv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tI have everything I need: both binding contracts, the eight published cross-bearings into Ch 11 (two section-pinned), Ch 10's four explicit handoff promises, the cached sources, and B1's seven sourced storage traps. One collision surfaced — **shipped Ch 10 has already told the reader CSI is the *last* of the four pluggable interfaces, while B6 calls it \"the third.\"**\n2\t\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t```\n6\t---\n7\tchapter: 11\n8\tchapter_type: \"content\"\n9\ttitle: \"Below the Waterline\"\n10\tsubtitle: \"Storage outlives the Pod that asked for it\"\n11\texam_domain: \"Container Orchestration (competency: Storage)\"\n12\tdomain_weight_pct: 5\n13\tcomplexity: \"mixed\"\n14\tnovelty: \"moderate\"\n15\tprereq_factor: \"heavy\"\n16\t\n17\t#-- SUBTITLE NOTE. The arc outline's working subtitle is \"Storage\n18\t#-- outlives the Pod that asked for it\" — eight words, inside this\n19\t#-- stage's ≤10-word constraint. Carried forward unmodified. It is also\n20\t#-- the §7 Zenith heading and the chapter's one-sentence thesis, so the\n21\t#-- three agree by construction rather than by coincidence.\n22\t\n23\t#-- EXAM_DOMAIN NOTE. D2.4 Storage, recorded in Ch 9/Ch 10's house form.\n24\t#-- Unlike Ch 10, this chapter has NO objective ambiguity: D2.4 is the\n25\t#-- only competency it touches and no concept in it is dual-listed.\n26\t#-- kb_tags carries the single objective ID.\n27\t#--\n28\t#-- The 5% figure is the chapter's AUTHORED allocation, not CNCF data.\n29\t#-- CNCF publishes four domain weights (44/28/16/12) and no\n30\t#-- sub-competency weights — B1 gap G33, B2 disclosure #1. The in-chapter\n31\t#-- metadata line must carry the published 28% for D2 with its source tag\n32\t#-- and the authored-allocation disclaimer, matching ch-02/-05/-07/-08/\n33\t#-- -09/-10 house form. Do not present 5% as published.\n34\t\n35\t#-- PREREQ NOTE. `heavy`, and the SHAPE of the dependency differs from\n36\t#-- Ch 10's in a way the Soundings rubric has to respect. Ch 10 was heavy\n37\t#-- because it needed ALL of Ch 9. This chapter is heavy because it needs\n38\t#-- narrow, specific pieces of SIX earlier chapters — Ch 2 §2 (the\n39\t#-- writable container layer), Ch 3 §6 (the control loop), Ch 4 §3\n40\t#-- (cluster-scoped) and §4 (ConfigMap/Secret), Ch 5 §1 (the Pod's shared\n41\t#-- context), Ch 6 §6 (StatefulSet identity), Ch 7 §2 (feasible nodes),\n42\t#-- Ch 10 §3 (the absent-component pattern). A reader who skipped any ONE\n43\t#-- of them loses one section, not the chapter.\n44\t#--\n45\t#-- Consequence for drafting: the Soundings 0–2 branch must NOT say \"go\n46\t#-- back and read Chapter N.\" It must name the specific sections, because\n47\t#-- the reader's gap is almost certainly narrow and telling them to\n48\t#-- re-read a whole chapter is both wrong and discouraging. This is the\n49\t#-- first chapter in the book where that distinction matters.\n50\t\n51\t#-- Section plan (no word budgets) ---------------------------------------\n52\t#-- Length is content-driven. Arc-outline depth band: \"standard\" — 5\n53\t#-- points. Planning signal only, NOT a target.\n54\t#--\n55\t#-- ⚠ SECTION NUMBERING IS LOAD-BEARING. Eight published cross-bearings\n56\t#-- point into this chapter and TWO name a section by number:\n57\t#--   chapter-05 line 349 → *[... see Ch 11 §1 — volume types and lifetimes]*\n58\t#--   chapter-09 line 758 → *[... see Ch 11 §6 — StatefulSets and their per-replica volume claims]*\n59\t#-- Both match the B6 skeleton exactly. §1 and §6 below are FIXED.\n60\t#-- The other six pointers name the chapter without a section and are\n61\t#-- free. Verified 2026-08-25 against chapters 01–10.\n62\tsections:\n63\t  - name: \"Three Lifetimes, and the Volumes That Have Them\"\n64\t    objectives: [\"D2.4\"]\n65\t    requires_figure: true\n66\t    figure_anchor: \"ch11-fig01-volume-lifetime-ladder\"\n67\t    checkpoint_after: false\n68\t  - name: \"The Claim and the Supply\"\n69\t    objectives: [\"D2.4\"]\n70\t    requires_figure: true\n71\t    figure_anchor: \"ch11-fig02-pv-pvc-storageclass-binding\"\n72\t    checkpoint_after: true\n73\t  - name: \"Provisioning on Demand\"\n74\t    objectives: [\"D2.4\"]\n75\t    requires_figure: true\n76\t    figure_anchor: \"ch11-fig03-static-vs-dynamic-provisioning\"\n77\t    checkpoint_after: false\n78\t  - name: \"Access Modes and What Happens After\"\n79\t    objectives: [\"D2.4\"]\n80\t    requires_figure: true\n81\t    figure_anchor: \"ch11-fig04-access-modes-and-reclaim-policies\"\n82\t    checkpoint_after: true\n83\t  - name: \"Who Actually Provides the Storage\"\n84\t    objectives: [\"D2.4\"]\n85\t    requires_figure: false\n86\t    figure_anchor: null\n87\t    checkpoint_after: false\n88\t  - name: \"Pods That Are Not Interchangeable, Revisited\"\n89\t    objectives: [\"D2.4\"]\n90\t    requires_figure: true\n91\t    figure_anchor: \"ch11-fig05-statefulset-pvc-pairing\"\n92\t    checkpoint_after: true\n93\t  - name: \"Outliving the Pod That Asked\"\n94\t    objectives: [\"D2.4\"]\n95\t    requires_figure: true\n96\t    figure_anchor: \"ch11-zenith-outliving-the-pod\"\n97\t    checkpoint_after: false\n98\t\n99\t#-- Seven sections against 5 weight points — one FEWER than Ch 9 and\n100\t#-- Ch 10, which both ran eight. Correct: this is a single arc, not two.\n101\t#-- §1 through §6 walk one ladder from the container filesystem to a\n102\t#-- claim that survives its cluster, and §7 states what the walk was for.\n103\t#-- No section here is a second subject the way Ch 10's §6–§7 were.\n104\t\n105\t#-- Skill v5.3 Part 11: Soundings pre-chapter diagnostic ------------------\n106\t#-- FIVE of the eight are retrieval from shipped chapters, which per B3's\n107\t#-- design note makes them spaced-retrieval events at zero cost against\n108\t#-- the retrieval budget. Three are general infrastructure priors, so a\n109\t#-- reader with storage