{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016kojKJxJX6BG9eXp3sLPUQ","type":"tool_result","content":"120\t    - \"general infrastructure prior — deleting a VM, and whether its attached disk goes with it; whether the answer depends on how the disk came to exist\"\n121\t    - \"general infrastructure prior — whether two machines can safely mount one block device read-write at the same time without a clustered filesystem\"\n122\t\n123\t#-- ✅ FIXED-POINT SPOILER CHECK — all eight cleared.\n124\t#-- The chapter's Fixed Points are: the three-lifetime ladder; PV is\n125\t#-- supply and PVC is demand and Pods reference claims never volumes;\n126\t#-- binding is exclusive and one-to-one; RWO counts NODES not Pods;\n127\t#-- dynamically-provisioned volumes inherit the StorageClass reclaim\n128\t#-- policy, which defaults to Delete; a StatefulSet's PVCs survive\n129\t#-- deletion of the Pod and of the StatefulSet; CSI closes the set of\n130\t#-- four. No question stem above states any of them.\n131\t#--   Q3 names PersistentVolume but asks ONLY about scope — which Ch 4\n132\t#--     taught, graded, and put in its Chapter Summary. It does not hint\n133\t#--     at the supply/demand split, which is §2's Fixed Point.\n134\t#--   Q5, Q7 and Q8 are deliberately posed OUTSIDE Kubernetes — arrays,\n135\t#--     VMs, block devices — so they build the priors that make §2 and §4\n136\t#--     land without pre-empting the Kubernetes-specific claims. Q8 in\n137\t#--     particular establishes the physical constraint that makes RWO\n138\t#--     sensible WITHOUT saying what unit RWO counts.\n139\t#--   Q4's answer previews the storage vocabulary, but only because\n140\t#--     shipped Ch 6 line 864 already previewed it in those exact terms.\n141\t#--     Nothing new is disclosed.\n142\t\n143\t#-- Skill v5.3 Part 8: practice-question budget ---------------------------\n144\t#-- B4 allocates 8 / 10 / 17 = 35 and states plainly that the Bearings\n145\t#-- figure is a minimum to exceed. Set at 15 across three checkpoints of\n146\t#-- 5, matching the shape shipped by Chapters 3–10 without exception.\n147\t#-- Chapter total 35 -> 40.\n148\tquestion_budget:\n149\t  soundings: 8\n150\t  taking_your_bearings: 15             # across 3 checkpoints (5 + 5 + 5)\n151\t  practice_questions: 17\n152\t  total_this_chapter: 40\n153\t\n154\t#-- Concept / objective / command tagging --------------------------------\n155\tkb_tags:\n156\t  objectives: [\"D2.4\"]\n157\t  concepts:\n158\t    - \"volume\"\n159\t    - \"volume-lifetime-ladder\"\n160\t    - \"ephemeral-volume\"\n161\t    - \"persistent-volume-lifetime\"\n162\t    - \"emptydir\"\n163\t    - \"emptydir-medium-memory\"\n164\t    - \"emptydir-size-limit\"\n165\t    - \"hostpath\"\n166\t    - \"hostpath-type-field\"\n167\t    - \"hostpath-security-risk\"\n168\t    - \"configmap-volume\"\n169\t    - \"secret-volume\"\n170\t    - \"secret-volume-tmpfs\"\n171\t    - \"projected-volume\"\n172\t    - \"downwardapi-volume\"\n173\t    - \"generic-ephemeral-volume\"\n174\t    - \"subpath\"\n175\t    - \"subpath-no-updates\"\n176\t    - \"nfs-volume\"\n177\t    - \"local-volume\"\n178\t    - \"persistentvolume\"\n179\t    - \"persistentvolumeclaim\"\n180\t    - \"supply-and-demand-split\"\n181\t    - \"pods-consume-node-resources\"\n182\t    - \"pvcs-consume-pv-resources\"\n183\t    - \"pv-lifecycle-independence\"\n184\t    - \"binding\"\n185\t    - \"exclusive-one-to-one-binding\"\n186\t    - \"unbound-claim\"\n187\t    - \"pv-phase\"\n188\t    - \"released-not-available\"\n189\t    - \"storageclass\"\n190\t    - \"static-provisioning\"\n191\t    - \"dynamic-provisioning\"\n192\t    - \"provisioner\"\n193\t    - \"storageclass-parameters\"\n194\t    - \"default-storageclass\"\n195\t    - \"empty-storage-class-opt-out\"\n196\t    - \"volume-binding-mode\"\n197\t    - \"wait-for-first-consumer\"\n198\t    - \"access-mode\"\n199\t    - \"readwriteonce\"\n200\t    - \"readonlymany\"\n201\t    - \